module examples.err_layout_wire_capability

# plans/M7.md item B, 03-hardware.md §3, verbatim: a `wire` layout is
# "persistent/network bytes — exact encoding independent of any target, no
# capabilities or target-dependent fields inside".
#
# Note what makes this rejection *live* today: no capability type exists
# yet (plans/M7.md item A mints `DeviceCap`/`Mmio`/`IrqCap`/`DmaPool`), so
# checked after name resolution this rule would be dead code and would
# report `error[name]: unknown name `DmaPool`` — a diagnostic naming the
# wrong cause. The `@layout` pass therefore runs *before* name resolution
# (`sema::types::check_layouts`), which is also why the message below
# names the capability rather than the missing name.

@layout(wire, endian=little)
struct Record:
    magic: u32
    payloads: DmaPool[Payloads, 4096]
